custodian — split license

Copyright (C) 2026 Heilar / Markús Thor and contributors

This repository is under two licenses. The split is by kind of file.

Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) covers
documentation, research notes, manifestos, and every other written
file. Attribution is required. That requirement is deliberate for a
civic project: reuse is welcome, and the source of the writing stays
visible.

CC BY 4.0 applies to everything that is not code. That includes:

- Paths: README.md, primitives.md, docs/, and any other prose added
  later (notes, outlines, specifications written as documents).
- File types: Markdown and other written formats, such as .md, .rst,
  .adoc, and .txt when the file is prose rather than a program,
  script, or configuration file.

The GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0) covers any code
that lands in this repository. AGPL-3.0 is used so that a modified
copy offered as a network service remains available to the people who
use it. That is the same auditability approach as Pol.is and ZKorum's
Agora.

AGPL-3.0 applies to code, which means source files, scripts, and
configs, wherever they sit in the tree:

- Source files, such as .py, .js, .ts, .tsx, .jsx, .go, .rs, .java,
  .c, .h, .cpp, and other programming-language sources.
- Scripts, such as shell scripts, Makefiles, and other files meant to
  be executed.
- Configs, such as .json, .yaml, .yml, .toml, .ini, Dockerfiles, and
  other configuration files.

There is no application source in the tree yet. When code is added, it
is under AGPL-3.0 only.

The license texts themselves are not project writing. Unmodified
verbatim copies are in this repository:

- LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International public license, from
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.txt
  Creative Commons dedicates that legal-code text to the public domain
  under CC0. The human-readable license page is
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
- LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt — GNU Affero General Public License, version 3,
  from https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt
  The Free Software Foundation permits verbatim copying of that
  document and does not allow changes to it. The license page is
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html

Those two files are the copies distributed with this project. They are
not paraphrases.
